  "notes": "96kHz remote I/O expander for A&H dLive, Avantis, SQ/SQ+, and 96kHz Qu digital mixing systems, and AHM matrix processors — not a standalone mixer, so mapped to Audio interface as the closest fit in the type enum. Ports confirmed against the manufacturer's official product page (allen-heath.com/hardware/everything-i-o/gx4816) and the official GX4816 Getting Started Guide (support.allen-heath.com). 48x XLR mic/line inputs (labeled \"Mic/Line In N\" here; front-panel silkscreen is numeric only) and 16x XLR line outputs are analog and ungraded. GX port explicitly documented as EtherCon over \"Gigabit Ethernet\" (grade eth-1g); DX1/DX2 ports explicitly documented as EtherCon over \"Fast Ethernet\" (grade eth-100m), each carrying 32x32 96kHz channels for daisy-chaining DX32/DX168/DX164-W/DX012 expanders. On SQ/Avantis only, DX2 can alternatively host an A&H ME Personal Mixing system (not supported on dLive/AHM). All three network-style ports use locking Neutrik EtherCon connectors, mapped to the \"ethercon\" connector id rather than plain rj45. Power is an IEC inlet (universal 100-240V AC PSU). Unit can also be used free-standing/off-rack; rackUnits reflects the 5U 19\" rack-mount form factor when installed.",
